    narr:narration """This narrative holds a settled ruling on reaction delivery: [one bundle per run per person rather than one message per skill](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_2), voiced as a person should get one thing to read, not four. The [boundary rule that a bundle closes when the run closes](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_3) was held against pushback on the batching window — a skill missing the close waits for the next run. The [rejected alternative of per-skill delivery with client-side collapsing](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_4) is recorded as moving the ordering problem onto the reader, with [the same rejection rationale stated separately](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_5). The arc opens with [the framing of where reaction delivery belongs](narr:Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_1) and is anchored by [the position on where bundling and batching windows should be bounded](narr:Position_ReactionDeliveryBundlingAndBatchingBoundary).""" ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_1> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_2> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_3> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_4> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_5> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Position_ReactionDeliveryBundlingAndBatchingBoundary> ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "we route every reaction through one bundle per run per person, not one\n> message per skill — a person should get one thing to read, not four" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_2> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "Tina pushed back on the batching window" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_3> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "Tanya held: the bundle closes when\nthe run closes, and a skill that misses the close waits for the next run rather\nthan sending on its own." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_4> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "The alternative considered and rejected was per-skill\ndelivery with client-side collapsing, which moves the ordering problem onto the\nreader." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_5> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "Pushback on the batching window was raised and held against — the close-on-run-close boundary survived challenge rather than being adjusted." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_3> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "The rejected road not taken: per-skill delivery with client-side collapsing, dismissed as shifting the ordering burden onto the reader." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_4> ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_5> ] ;
    narr:voiceTrait [ narr:dim "conviction" ; narr:reading "decision-grade — positions are voiced as rulings, not open claims" ; narr:text "we route every reaction through one bundle per run per person, not one\n> message per skill — a person should get one thing to read, not four" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_2> ] ;
    narr:voiceTrait [ narr:dim "power" ; narr:reading "legitimate authority — the ruling is issued from role, then defended on its merits" ; narr:text "Tanya (team owner) ruled on where reaction delivery belongs:" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_1> ] ;
    narr:voiceTrait [ narr:dim "relational" ; narr:reading "authority-ranking — deference is structured around who holds the decision" ; narr:text "Tina pushed back on the batching window and Tanya held: the bundle closes when\nthe run closes, and a skill that misses the close waits for the next run rather\nthan sending on its own." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_2DeliveryRoutingRulingE2ESynthetic_3> ] ;
